{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LyyR2iJVgLu91rBTzG742z","type":"tool_result","content":"commit bf297a4fca04023f0e783e13a28713a4ab1ace5c\nAuthor: Reviewer <reviewer@example.test>\nDate:   Wed Nov 4 17:22:49 2026 -0600\n\n    spine: WI-994's arms-map edits: LLR-365 drops the clause no test or case reaches and states the repeat rule, and TC-406 states the next-line wrap\n    \n    WI: WI-994\n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n    Loop-Session: 20261104T181017Z-49d2cc\n    Bar-Green: tree=443beffcbfac76959e0d50148bfd89d5afac5c9c work=2bcca3208e1818fdcd840409d9595660dcc9596f bar=review tests=03f6ea99b8a6e2a1c14cddd9801647749768ea1f7822b21715ec27def523f31d review bar PASS (4 named tests)\n    Loop-Session: 20261104T181017Z-49d2cc\n\ndiff --git a/docs/decisions/wi-994.toml b/docs/decisions/wi-994.toml\nindex 1a02c8bbf..743e3eb66 100644\n--- a/docs/decisions/wi-994.toml\n+++ b/docs/decisions/wi-994.toml\n@@ -24,3 +24,10 @@ alternative = \"Send the two code MINORs to successor rows; each would be a new r\n reversal_cost = \"Low: small changes inside the spec's surface, reviewed at the gate.\"\n why_not_escalated = \"Triage is the coordinator's; the gate reviews the tip that lands.\"\n review = \"\"\n+\n+[decision.D-004]\n+decided = \"The arms map found 30 arms and 4 gaps at the reconcile tip, closed in one Terra turn. LLR-365's clause `A declaration can only add a finding` is removed: it states authority, no test exercises it and no TC states it, and the spec's Trust section is its home; the plan's P1 named the clause, and the Done-when does not, so the row departs from the plan's row sketch here. TC-406 now states the next-line wrap, and LLR-365 states that a test repeating its module's test case is no finding.\"\n+alternative = \"Keep the clause and add a test for a negative, which would pin nothing a reader of the code cannot see.\"\n+reversal_cost = \"Low: one clause of a Drafted row, judged at the sitting.\"\n+why_not_escalated = \"Spine text is judged at the sitting that follows; recorded for confirm or overrule.\"\n+review = \"\"\ndiff --git a/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml b/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\nindex 038e5a384..f177c6b5f 100644\n--- a/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\n+++ b/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\n@@ -1561,7 +1561,7 @@ sr_refs = [\"SR-157\"]\n title = \"Test-file declarations of their test cases\"\n module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/gen_arch_map.py;project-trajectory/scripts/trajectory_arch.py\"\n code_symbol = \"read_test_tags/tc_tag_findings\"\n-detail = \"A test-file back-link declaration names only the test cases it runs. In a Python test file, declarations in the module docstring and in a test's docstring are read; in another supported test-file type, declarations are read at file level. A byte-order mark at the start of a file does not change its reading. The two Python levels union. A non-docstring string literal, a backtick-quoted token and an unsupported test-file type make no declaration. A declaration outside a read position, including a pytest-fixture docstring, is refused as misplaced. The following are refused as malformed: a declaration whose list is not test-case ids only; a read-position line whose token follows prose and names a test case; and a next line that continues a valid list. The after-prose refusal directs the declaration to the start of its own line. An id absent from the live test-case registry, including an example or retired id, is refused as unknown; a Drafted test case is live. A test file that cannot be decoded or parsed is refused as unreadable. Every live id in a valid declaration maps to its test node. Each refusal names the repository-relative file, line and shape. A declaration can only add a finding, and reading test files does not change source-file declaration reading. No tests root or test-case registry is vacuous. Findings warn without